From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leonardo Capossio <capossio.leonardo@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: linker: place TEXT_SECTIONS snippets in .text

zephyr_linker_sources(TEXT_SECTIONS ...) had no effect on RISC-V,
whose linker script never included the snippets file. Include it at the
start of .text, after __text_region_start and ahead of the catch-all
input patterns, so that a snippet can gather functions into one place,
for instance to keep a hot path from conflicting with itself in a small
direct-mapped instruction cache.

ROM_START can also hold such a list, but it lies before
__text_region_start, and the stack unwinder and the perf backend reject
return addresses outside the text region: functions placed there drop
out of stack traces.

Signed-off-by: Leonardo Capossio <capossio.leonardo@gmail.com>
---
 include/zephyr/arch/riscv/common/linker.ld | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/zephyr/arch/riscv/common/linker.ld b/include/zephyr/arch/riscv/common/linker.ld
index c1314e9..a8d5aa6 100644
--- a/include/zephyr/arch/riscv/common/linker.ld
+++ b/include/zephyr/arch/riscv/common/linker.ld
@@ -180,6 +180,12 @@ SECTIONS
 
 		__text_region_start = .;
 
+/* Located in generated directory. This file is populated by calling
+ * zephyr_linker_sources(TEXT_SECTIONS ...). Ahead of the catch-all
+ * patterns below, so that it can claim input sections of its own.
+ */
+#include <snippets-text-sections.ld>
+
 		*(.text)
 		*(".text.*")
 		*(.gnu.linkonce.t.*)
-- 
2.52.0.windows.1

